<section>
    <h2>What is Artificial Intelligence?</h2>
    <article>
        <h3>Overview</h3>
        <p>
            Artificial Intelligence (AI) is the field of computing focused on building systems that can
            perform tasks that usually require human intelligence. These tasks can include understanding
            language, recognizing patterns, making predictions, and learning from experience.
        </p>
        <p>
            In software development, AI is used in tools that help write code, detect bugs, recommend solutions,
            and automate repetitive work. AI can also power features inside apps, such as search suggestions,
            image recognition, and personalized recommendations.
        </p>
    </article>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>How is AI Used in Software</h2>
    <article>
        <h3>Common Uses</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Code assistance (autocomplete, refactoring suggestions)</li>
            <li>Bug detection and automated testing support</li>
            <li>Fraud detection and security monitoring</li>
            <li>Recommendations and personalization in apps</li>
            <li>Chatbots and customer support automation</li>
        </ul>
        <img src="/img/ai-overview.jpg" alt="Illustration representing artificial intelligence">
    </article>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Why It Matters</h2>
    <article>
        <h3>Importance of AI</h3>
        <p>
            AI can improve software quality and productivity by helping developers work faster and catch issues earlier.
            At the same time, AI systems must be designed carefully to avoid mistakes, bias, and privacy risks.
        </p>
    </article>
</section>

